on-arrival: e21_after_done = 1

= Levi's Letter

The strike in Central Germany was lost, but it was a strike and not a putsch, and Levi knows the difference. He writes a long letter to Lenin. The strike was right, he says, and badly prepared: the party asked the workers to fight before it had won them. He asks for one thing, that the International stop sending envoys who decide German questions in hotel rooms.

[? if e21_levi_resigned = 1 : He has been out of the Zentrale since February. His friends say it is time he came back. ?][? if e21_levi_resigned = 0 : He still holds the chair, and the Left says the defeat is his, since he would not let the party fight properly. ?]

- @return: Bring Levi back to the head of the party.
- @counsel: Keep the present leadership, and listen to him.
- @sideline: Push him to the edge of the party.

@return
subtitle: Levi takes the chair on condition that the emissaries go home. Zinoviev will not forget it.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e21_levi_fate = 5;
Q.leading_faction = 'luxemburgist';
Q.junior_faction = 'unionist';
Q.e21_levi_resigned = 0;
RG.setRole('levi', 'Chairman of the Zentrale');
RG.ecci('zinoviev', -8);
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 3;
!}

The Central Committee asks Levi and Zetkin to come back. Levi takes the chair, and Kun leaves Berlin in a temper.

@counsel
subtitle: Brandler leads, Levi advises. The theory of the offensive is dropped.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e21_levi_fate = 5;
if (Q.leading_faction == 'offensive') {
    Q.leading_faction = 'unionist';
    Q.junior_faction = 'offensive';
}
Q.lean_unionist += 2;
!}

The Zentrale keeps its leaders and changes its tone. The word "offensive" disappears from the Rote Fahne, and Levi's letter is circulated to the Central Committee.

@sideline
subtitle: The Left will be pleased. His friends will take his case to Moscow.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e21_levi_fate = 2;
Q.luxemburgist_satisfaction -= 12;
Q.lean_offensive += 2;
!}

The Zentrale resolves that the strike failed because it was not bold enough. Levi is removed from every committee he still sits on.
